{
  "name": "02 - Telegram Bot v2",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 02 - Telegram Bot (v2, natural language)\n- **Customer just says hi** → bot asks them to share their phone (📱 button) → finds their orders\n- **Order link** still works (t.me/bot?start=ORD123)\n- **Buttons** confirm / cancel\n- **Plain text** works too: \"yes confirm it\", \"cancel my order\", \"where is my order\", \"I want to return it\"\n- **/admin** in the owner's group makes it the owner chat (alerts go there)\n\nSecurity: phone must be the sender's own (Telegram-verified); orders can only be changed by their owner.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "b5ca90bc-bb55-43d7-8847-35c22c325da3",
      "name": "Note v2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -520,
        -80
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "updates": [
          "message",
          "callback_query"
        ],
        "additionalFields": {}
      },
      "id": "1f42c26d-b263-464f-a1f3-22a7d4ef899f",
      "name": "Telegram Trigger",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.telegramTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        0,
        400
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "telegramApi": {
          "id": "2",
          "name": "Telegram account"
        }
      },
      "webhookId": "b0f2a0e8-9ffb-4a86-b26d-782dd7d398a7"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "// Work out what kind of Telegram update this is.\nconst u = $json;\n\n// Button press (Confirm / Cancel)\nif (u.callback_query) {\n  const cq = u.callback_query;\n  const [action, order_number] = String(cq.data || '').split(':');\n  return { json: { type: 'button', chat_id: cq.message.chat.id, action, order_number, callback_id: cq.id } };\n}\n\nconst m = u.message || {};\nconst chat_id = m.chat?.id;\nif (!chat_id) return { json: { type: 'ignore' } };\nconst isPrivate = (m.chat?.type || 'private') === 'private';\n\n// Customer shared a phone number with the 📱 button.\n// Only trust it if the contact is the sender's own number.\nif (m.contact) {\n  const verified = !!m.contact.user_id && m.contact.user_id === m.from?.id;\n  return { json: { type: 'contact', chat_id, phone: String(m.contact.phone_number || ''), verified } };\n}\n\n// \"/admin@MyBot\" -> \"/admin\"\nconst text = (m.text || '').trim().replace(/^(\\/\\w+)@\\S+/, '$1');\nif (!text) return { json: { type: 'ignore' } };\n\nif (text === '/admin') return { json: { type: 'admin', chat_id } };\n\n// In the owner's group, ignore everything except /admin\nif (!isPrivate) return { json: { type: 'ignore' } };\n\n// Order link: t.me/bot?start=ORD123 sends \"/start ORD123\"\nconst start = text.match(/^\\/start\\s+(\\S+)/);\nif (start) return { json: { type: 'start', chat_id, order_number: start[1] } };\n\n// Everything else is a normal chat message (\"/start\" alone = \"Hi\")\nreturn { json: { type: 'chat', chat_id, text: text === '/start' ? 'Hi' : text } };"
      },
